    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 all 3 tests pass. The build compiles (DTOs regenerated with the new `email` field, MapStruct mapper regenerated) and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the optional owner `email` rule: present \u21d2 must be syntactically valid, stored/returned lower-cased; absent \u21d2 accepted; present-but-invalid \u21d2 400.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` (and MapStruct mapper) now carry `email`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` field/column with getter/setter.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a nullable `email` column to `owners`; fixed the hsqldb seed `data.sql` inserts to name their columns (the column-less `VALUES` form broke on the new column \u2014 this was the initial context-load failure).\n- **`NormalizeOwnerEmail.java`** (new function) \u2014 treats blank/missing as absent, validates syntax via regex, and mutates the body's email to lower-case in place; throws the checked `InvalidEmailException` when present-but-invalid.\n- **`InvalidEmailException` + `InvalidEmailHandler` + escalation YAML** \u2014 map that exception to a 400, following the existing `InvalidTelephone` pattern.\n- **Pipelines** \u2014 inserted the `normalizeEmail` step into `owners.POST.yml`; also wired it into `{ownerId}.PUT.yml` and added `owner.setEmail(...)` to `ApplyOwner` so updates honor the same rule (spec is \"an owner\", not just creation).\n\nThe three acceptance tests (lowercasing, invalid\u2192400, missing\u21922xx) and the full suite pass.\n\nOne note for your awareness: the create path validates/normalizes email in a dedicated function step rather than via `@Valid` bean validation, matching how telephone is already handled in this codebase \u2014 so the 400 comes back as a plain-text message body, consistent with `InvalidTelephoneHandler`.",
